<h2><span class="mw-headline" id="Fenod.27s_Weapons_-_3rd_Place">Fenod's Weapons - 3rd Place</span></h2>
<h3><span class="mw-headline" id="Lunacy.28Dagger.29_by_Fenod">Lunacy(Dagger) by Fenod</span></h3>
<ul><li> <b><a rel="nofollow" class="external text" href="http://www.dragonagenexus.com/downloads/file.php?id=2018">Dragon Age Nexus project page</a></b></li></ul>
<dl><dd>Many who saw the previous owner of this fine blade in battle thought he was insane. He was </dd>
<dd>the leader of a group of thugs in Denerim who claimed to be fearless. To set an example for </dd>
<dd>his men the commander would always fight blindfolded with wax plugging up his ears.  It turns </dd>
<dd>out he truly was mad and met his end when he ran into a volley of arrows...fired from  his own men.</dd></dl>
<p><br />
<a href="https://github.com/adarec1994/DragonAgeToolset/wiki/File%20-%20CC6Lunacy.jpg" title="Toolset Appearance"><img alt="Toolset Appearance" src="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/adarec1994/DragonAgeToolset/main/Wiki/assets/mw/images/8/81/CC6Lunacy.jpg" width="129" height="412" srcset="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/adarec1994/DragonAgeToolset/main/Wiki/assets/mw/images/8/81/CC6Lunacy.jpg 1.5x, https://raw.githubusercontent.com/adarec1994/DragonAgeToolset/main/Wiki/assets/mw/images/8/81/CC6Lunacy.jpg 2x" /></a>
<a href="https://github.com/adarec1994/DragonAgeToolset/wiki/File%20-%20Ingame.jpg" title="In Game Appearance"><img alt="In Game Appearance" src="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/adarec1994/DragonAgeToolset/main/Wiki/assets/mw/images/7/75/Ingame.jpg" width="400" height="411" srcset="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/adarec1994/DragonAgeToolset/main/Wiki/assets/mw/images/7/75/Ingame.jpg 1.5x, https://raw.githubusercontent.com/adarec1994/DragonAgeToolset/main/Wiki/assets/mw/images/7/75/Ingame.jpg 2x" /></a>
</p><p><br />
</p>
<h3><span class="mw-headline" id="Dreadscale.28Battleaxe.29_by_Fenod">Dreadscale(Battleaxe) by Fenod</span></h3>
<ul><li> <b><a rel="nofollow" class="external text" href="http://www.dragonagenexus.com/downloads/file.php?id=2017">Dragon Age Nexus project page</a></b></li></ul>
<dl><dd>This weapon is not crafted from scales of any sort, instead  </dd>
<dd>it has been fashioned from obsidian.  Dreadscale's name  </dd>
<dd>comes from numerous number of dragons that it has slain.  </dd>
<dd>It is no surprise then that in this age, the Dragon Age, </dd>
<dd>many believe it to have an enchantment which allows the</dd>
<dd>one who wields it to strike with enough force to cleave a</dd>
<dd>dragon in twain.</dd></dl>
<dl><dd>Whatever enchantment it possesses does not seem to </dd>
<dd>increase its effectiveness in killing dragons.  This has </dd>
<dd>become increasingly apparent as fool after fool has met</dd>
<dd>their end trying to best dragons while wielding Dreadscale.</dd>
<dd>That is not to say that it is not a formidable weapon, for in</dd>
<dd>the right hands Dreadscale is truly a sight to behold.</dd></dl>
<p><br />
<a href="https://github.com/adarec1994/DragonAgeToolset/wiki/File%20-%20CC6Dread.jpg" title="Toolset Appearance"><img alt="Toolset Appearance" src="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/adarec1994/DragonAgeToolset/main/Wiki/assets/mw/images/8/81/CC6Dread.jpg" width="130" height="413" srcset="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/adarec1994/DragonAgeToolset/main/Wiki/assets/mw/images/8/81/CC6Dread.jpg 1.5x, https://raw.githubusercontent.com/adarec1994/DragonAgeToolset/main/Wiki/assets/mw/images/8/81/CC6Dread.jpg 2x" /></a>
<a href="https://github.com/adarec1994/DragonAgeToolset/wiki/File%20-%20Dreadscale.jpg" title="In Game Appearance"><img alt="In Game Appearance" src="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/adarec1994/DragonAgeToolset/main/Wiki/assets/mw/images/9/9b/Dreadscale.jpg" width="400" height="411" srcset="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/adarec1994/DragonAgeToolset/main/Wiki/assets/mw/images/9/9b/Dreadscale.jpg 1.5x, https://raw.githubusercontent.com/adarec1994/DragonAgeToolset/main/Wiki/assets/mw/images/9/9b/Dreadscale.jpg 2x" /></a>
</p><p><br />
</p>
<h3><span class="mw-headline" id="Deadweight.28Maul.29_by_Fenod">Deadweight(Maul) by Fenod</span></h3>
<ul><li> <b><a rel="nofollow" class="external text" href="http://www.dragonagenexus.com/downloads/file.php?id=2016">Dragon Age Nexus project page</a></b></li></ul>
<dl><dd>Every time the story of this weapon's origin is told it varies </dd>
<dd>to a great degree.  The current telling of the tale claims that </dd>
<dd>the weapon originally belonged to a scrawny stonecutter in </dd>
<dd>Denerim by the name of Rupert.  Rupert had grown weary</dd>
<dd>of cutting stone and so he sought to join the city guard.</dd>
<dd>The problem was the guard captain told him he had no place </dd>
<dd>wielding a weapon and that he would only injure himself or </dd>
<dd>the other guards.  Rupert would show up every year and </dd>
<dd>try to join and each time he was turned away.</dd></dl>
<dl><dd>Eventually the guard captain realized that Rupert would </dd>
<dd>not cease so he had a crude maul fashioned from rock and</dd>
<dd>told Rupert that if he could wield it he would be allowed to </dd>
<dd>join the city guard.  Of course the captain did not expect</dd>
<dd>Rupert to attempt the feat, but much to his dismay Rupert</dd>
<dd>bent down, gripping the rock.</dd></dl>
<dl><dd>The guard captain looked on in astonishment as Rupert</dd>
<dd>hefted the ungainly weapon over his head, only to have it</dd>
<dd>fall onto him, crushing him.  Such is the tale of Rupert and </dd>
<dd>his weapon, aptly named Deadweight.  </dd></dl>
<p><br />
<a href="https://github.com/adarec1994/DragonAgeToolset/wiki/File%20-%20CC6Deadweight.jpg" title="Toolset Appearance"><img alt="Toolset Appearance" src="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/adarec1994/DragonAgeToolset/main/Wiki/assets/mw/images/4/41/CC6Deadweight.jpg" width="129" height="409" srcset="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/adarec1994/DragonAgeToolset/main/Wiki/assets/mw/images/4/41/CC6Deadweight.jpg 1.5x, https://raw.githubusercontent.com/adarec1994/DragonAgeToolset/main/Wiki/assets/mw/images/4/41/CC6Deadweight.jpg 2x" /></a>
<a href="https://github.com/adarec1994/DragonAgeToolset/wiki/File%20-%20Deadweight.jpg" title="In Game Appearance"><img alt="In Game Appearance" src="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/adarec1994/DragonAgeToolset/main/Wiki/assets/mw/images/e/e0/Deadweight.jpg" width="400" height="411" srcset="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/adarec1994/DragonAgeToolset/main/Wiki/assets/mw/images/e/e0/Deadweight.jpg 1.5x, https://raw.githubusercontent.com/adarec1994/DragonAgeToolset/main/Wiki/assets/mw/images/e/e0/Deadweight.jpg 2x" /></a>
</p><p><br />
</p>
<h3><span class="mw-headline" id="Barbarous_Mace_by_Fenod">Barbarous Mace by Fenod</span></h3>
<ul><li> <b><a rel="nofollow" class="external text" href="http://www.dragonagenexus.com/downloads/file.php?id=2015">Dragon Age Nexus project page</a></b></li></ul>
<dl><dd>This crude weapon appears to be Chasind, but has no  </dd>
<dd>legends to its name and bears no unique markings,   </dd>
<dd>nonetheless its effectiveness cannot be denied when in </dd>
<dd>capable hands.  The ensuing carnage is enough to paralyze</dd>
<dd>foes with fear.</dd></dl>
<p><br />
<a href="https://github.com/adarec1994/DragonAgeToolset/wiki/File%20-%20CC6BarbarousMace.jpg" title="Toolset Appearance"><img alt="Toolset Appearance" src="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/adarec1994/DragonAgeToolset/main/Wiki/assets/mw/images/9/93/CC6BarbarousMace.jpg" width="125" height="413" srcset="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/adarec1994/DragonAgeToolset/main/Wiki/assets/mw/images/9/93/CC6BarbarousMace.jpg 1.5x, https://raw.githubusercontent.com/adarec1994/DragonAgeToolset/main/Wiki/assets/mw/images/9/93/CC6BarbarousMace.jpg 2x" /></a>
<a href="https://github.com/adarec1994/DragonAgeToolset/wiki/File%20-%20BarbarousMace.jpg" title="In Game Appearance"><img alt="In Game Appearance" src="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/adarec1994/DragonAgeToolset/main/Wiki/assets/mw/images/d/de/BarbarousMace.jpg" width="400" height="411" srcset="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/adarec1994/DragonAgeToolset/main/Wiki/assets/mw/images/d/de/BarbarousMace.jpg 1.5x, https://raw.githubusercontent.com/adarec1994/DragonAgeToolset/main/Wiki/assets/mw/images/d/de/BarbarousMace.jpg 2x" /></a>
</p><p><br />
</p>
<h3><span class="mw-headline" id="Bonemaw_by_Fenod">Bonemaw by Fenod</span></h3>
<ul><li> <b><a rel="nofollow" class="external text" href="http://www.dragonagenexus.com/downloads/file.php?id=2014">Dragon Age Nexus project page</a></b></li></ul>
<dl><dd>This macabre weapon was carved from the bone of a high  </dd>
<dd>dragon, sharpened so that it can be wielded as a crude </dd>
<dd>blade.  The name of the smith that created the blade and </dd>
<dd>why it was made in such a manner has been lost to time.</dd>
<dd>With each passing age it finds a new name, in this age it is</dd>
<dd>known as Bonemaw.</dd></dl>
<dl><dd>Unlike a refined dragonbone blade Bonemaw is misshapen</dd>
<dd>and unwieldy.  Those who have seen it wielded in battle</dd>
<dd>claim that it can fell a pride demon in one swing though such</dd>
<dd>claims are naught but fanciful tales, giving the blade a </dd>
<dd>legendary status of sorts.</dd></dl>
<dl><dd>While it may not dispatch a Pride demon in a single blow </dd>
<dd>there is no denying that the blade is indeed a formidable</dd>
<dd>weapon.  If you find yourself pitted against an opponent </dd>
<dd>wielding this weapon it is advisable that you flee.  You are</dd>
<dd>lucky then that you find it in your hands. </dd></dl>
<p><br />
<a href="https://github.com/adarec1994/DragonAgeToolset/wiki/File%20-%20CC6Bonemaw.jpg" title="Toolset Appearance"><img alt="Toolset Appearance" src="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/adarec1994/DragonAgeToolset/main/Wiki/assets/mw/images/b/b6/CC6Bonemaw.jpg" width="129" height="410" srcset="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/adarec1994/DragonAgeToolset/main/Wiki/assets/mw/images/b/b6/CC6Bonemaw.jpg 1.5x, https://raw.githubusercontent.com/adarec1994/DragonAgeToolset/main/Wiki/assets/mw/images/b/b6/CC6Bonemaw.jpg 2x" /></a>
<a href="https://github.com/adarec1994/DragonAgeToolset/wiki/File%20-%20Bonemaw.jpg" title="In Game Appearance"><img alt="In Game Appearance" src="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/adarec1994/DragonAgeToolset/main/Wiki/assets/mw/images/c/cf/Bonemaw.jpg" width="505" height="408" srcset="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/adarec1994/DragonAgeToolset/main/Wiki/assets/mw/images/c/cf/Bonemaw.jpg 1.5x, https://raw.githubusercontent.com/adarec1994/DragonAgeToolset/main/Wiki/assets/mw/images/c/cf/Bonemaw.jpg 2x" /></a>
</p><p><br />
</p>
<h3><span class="mw-headline" id="Malice.28Dagger.29_by_Fenod">Malice(Dagger) by Fenod</span></h3>
<ul><li> <b><a rel="nofollow" class="external text" href="http://www.dragonagenexus.com/downloads/file.php?id=2013">Dragon Age Nexus project page</a></b></li></ul>
<dl><dd>Malice's construction is simple, similar to Chasind weapons</dd>
<dd>though much cruder in design.  It's blade is fitted to a metal</dd>
<dd>bar which is in turn fitted to the weapon's basket hilt. It is  </dd>
<dd>one of the last known weapons to be forged from the same</dd>
<dd>ore as the greatsword Agony.  The name of the ore has</dd>
<dd>been lost to the ages along with it's exact properties.</dd></dl>
<dl><dd>It is apparent  that the ore can be heated to extreme</dd>
<dd>temperatures without it melting.  Surprisingly, wielding the</dd>
<dd>weapon will not cause injury as the heat that it gives off is</dd>
<dd>similar in nature to the effect of a fire enchantment.   </dd></dl>
<p><br />
<a href="https://github.com/adarec1994/DragonAgeToolset/wiki/File%20-%20CC6Malice.jpg" title="Toolset Appearance"><img alt="Toolset Appearance" src="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/adarec1994/DragonAgeToolset/main/Wiki/assets/mw/images/9/95/CC6Malice.jpg" width="180" height="404" srcset="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/adarec1994/DragonAgeToolset/main/Wiki/assets/mw/images/9/95/CC6Malice.jpg 1.5x, https://raw.githubusercontent.com/adarec1994/DragonAgeToolset/main/Wiki/assets/mw/images/9/95/CC6Malice.jpg 2x" /></a>
<a href="https://github.com/adarec1994/DragonAgeToolset/wiki/File%20-%20Malice.jpg" title="In Game Appearance"><img alt="In Game Appearance" src="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/adarec1994/DragonAgeToolset/main/Wiki/assets/mw/images/a/aa/Malice.jpg" width="317" height="404" srcset="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/adarec1994/DragonAgeToolset/main/Wiki/assets/mw/images/a/aa/Malice.jpg 1.5x, https://raw.githubusercontent.com/adarec1994/DragonAgeToolset/main/Wiki/assets/mw/images/a/aa/Malice.jpg 2x" /></a>
</p><p><br />
</p>
<h3><span class="mw-headline" id="Pestilence_by_Fenod">Pestilence by Fenod</span></h3>
<ul><li> <b><a rel="nofollow" class="external text" href="http://www.dragonagenexus.com/downloads/file.php?id=2012">Dragon Age Nexus project page</a></b></li></ul>
<dl><dd>It is believed that the axe known as Pestilence was taken </dd>
<dd>from the fade where it is difficult to discern living beings </dd>
<dd>from inanimate objects.  This axe is one such object.  It is  </dd>
<dd>covered in flesh and yet by all appearances it behaves just </dd>
<dd>as any axe would.</dd></dl>
<dl><dd>As if this were not peculiar enough it increases the skill of </dd>
<dd>whomever wields it.  While it is widely assumed that this is</dd>
<dd>because the weapon is enchanted a few believe that the</dd>
<dd>weapon is alive and guides the hand of those who wield it.</dd>
<dd>It's edge is coated with poison leading some to believe that</dd>
<dd>the axe itself secretes the poison.  Whether or not this </dd>
<dd>presumption is valid there is no mistaking the foul nature of</dd>
<dd>the poison.</dd></dl>
<p><br />
<a href="https://github.com/adarec1994/DragonAgeToolset/wiki/File%20-%20CC6Pestilence.jpg" title="Toolset Appearance"><img alt="Toolset Appearance" src="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/adarec1994/DragonAgeToolset/main/Wiki/assets/mw/images/b/ba/CC6Pestilence.jpg" width="129" height="409" srcset="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/adarec1994/DragonAgeToolset/main/Wiki/assets/mw/images/b/ba/CC6Pestilence.jpg 1.5x, https://raw.githubusercontent.com/adarec1994/DragonAgeToolset/main/Wiki/assets/mw/images/b/ba/CC6Pestilence.jpg 2x" /></a>
<a href="https://github.com/adarec1994/DragonAgeToolset/wiki/File%20-%20Pestilence.jpg" title="In Game Appearance"><img alt="In Game Appearance" src="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/adarec1994/DragonAgeToolset/main/Wiki/assets/mw/images/3/39/Pestilence.jpg" width="320" height="408" srcset="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/adarec1994/DragonAgeToolset/main/Wiki/assets/mw/images/3/39/Pestilence.jpg 1.5x, https://raw.githubusercontent.com/adarec1994/DragonAgeToolset/main/Wiki/assets/mw/images/3/39/Pestilence.jpg 2x" /></a>
</p><p><br />
</p>
<h3><span class="mw-headline" id="Lament_by_Fenod">Lament by Fenod</span></h3>
<ul><li> <b><a rel="nofollow" class="external text" href="http://www.dragonagenexus.com/downloads/file.php?id=2011">Dragon Age Nexus project page</a></b></li></ul>
<dl><dd>The name of the original owner of this blade is long forgotten </dd>
<dd>but it is said that she loved battle so much that she would seek  </dd>
<dd>it out all across Ferelden.  Her skill with a blade was exceptional,  </dd>
<dd>but it was the blade which she wielded that made her a legend. She</dd>
<dd>called the blade Lament, in honor of those that fell in battle, </dd>
<dd>enemies and allies alike.</dd></dl>
<dl><dd>She believed that death fueled the blade and give her the</dd>
<dd>will to fight even when all those around her had fallen.</dd>
<dd>Those who saw her in battle claimed that with every swing </dd>
<dd>the blade would let out a cry.  Today it is known that the</dd>
<dd>blade has no such enchantment though it is noted that the </dd>
<dd>blade does indeed bear an enchantment of an unknown nature. </dd></dl>
<p><br />  
<a href="https://github.com/adarec1994/DragonAgeToolset/wiki/File%20-%20CC6Lament.jpg" title="Toolset Appearance"><img alt="Toolset Appearance" src="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/adarec1994/DragonAgeToolset/main/Wiki/assets/mw/images/f/f7/CC6Lament.jpg" width="129" height="410" srcset="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/adarec1994/DragonAgeToolset/main/Wiki/assets/mw/images/f/f7/CC6Lament.jpg 1.5x, https://raw.githubusercontent.com/adarec1994/DragonAgeToolset/main/Wiki/assets/mw/images/f/f7/CC6Lament.jpg 2x" /></a>
<a href="https://github.com/adarec1994/DragonAgeToolset/wiki/File%20-%20Lament.jpg" title="In Game Appearance"><img alt="In Game Appearance" src="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/adarec1994/DragonAgeToolset/main/Wiki/assets/mw/images/7/7a/Lament.jpg" width="509" height="411" srcset="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/adarec1994/DragonAgeToolset/main/Wiki/assets/mw/images/7/7a/Lament.jpg 1.5x, https://raw.githubusercontent.com/adarec1994/DragonAgeToolset/main/Wiki/assets/mw/images/7/7a/Lament.jpg 2x" /></a>
</p><p><br />
</p>
<h2><span class="mw-headline" id="Knotwood_Staff_Helekanalaith_-_Best_Newcomer">Knotwood Staff Helekanalaith - Best Newcomer</span></h2>
<ul><li> <b><a rel="nofollow" class="external text" href="http://dragonagenexus.com/downloads/file.php?id=2020">Dragon Age Nexus project page</a></b></li></ul>
<dl><dd>This gnarled staff's origin can be traced back to the Knotwood Hills. No doubt it once belonged to a hangman's tree or worse; a darkspawn scratching pole!</dd></dl>
<p><br />
<a href="https://github.com/adarec1994/DragonAgeToolset/wiki/File%20-%20Kntwdstf1.png" title="Fight fire."><img alt="Fight fire." src="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/adarec1994/DragonAgeToolset/main/Wiki/assets/mw/images/c/ce/Kntwdstf1.png" width="400" height="400" srcset="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/adarec1994/DragonAgeToolset/main/Wiki/assets/mw/images/c/ce/Kntwdstf1.png 1.5x, https://raw.githubusercontent.com/adarec1994/DragonAgeToolset/main/Wiki/assets/mw/images/c/ce/Kntwdstf1.png 2x" /></a>
<a href="https://github.com/adarec1994/DragonAgeToolset/wiki/File%20-%20Kntwdstf2.png" title="With fire!"><img alt="With fire!" src="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/adarec1994/DragonAgeToolset/main/Wiki/assets/mw/images/a/ab/Kntwdstf2.png" width="400" height="400" srcset="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/adarec1994/DragonAgeToolset/main/Wiki/assets/mw/images/a/ab/Kntwdstf2.png 1.5x, https://raw.githubusercontent.com/adarec1994/DragonAgeToolset/main/Wiki/assets/mw/images/a/ab/Kntwdstf2.png 2x" /></a>
</p><p><br />
</p>
<h2><span class="mw-headline" id="Dagger_of_Ashyera.27s_Cult_by_Gisle_Aune">Dagger of Ashyera's Cult by Gisle Aune</span></h2>
<p><b><a rel="nofollow" class="external text" href="http://www.dragonagenexus.com/downloads/file.php?id=2038">Dragon Age Nexus project page</a></b>
</p><p>These daggers - allthough scarce in number in Ferelden - are quite common located within a cult in some small state in the Free Marches. (for usage in my mod The Dark Deal (WIP))
</p><p>Bonuses: +2 damage, +6 attack
Material: Silverite.
</p><p>Note: I was granted extra time by Mikemike57 - sorry for delivering almost too late.
